144:## How compatible is mise with asdf?
145-
146:mise should be able to read/install any `.tool-versions` file used by asdf. Any asdf plugin
147-should be usable in mise. The commands in mise are slightly
148:different, such as `mise install node@20.0.0` vs `asdf install node 20.0.0`—this is so
149:multiple tools can be specified at once. However, asdf-style syntax is still supported (`mise
150-install node 20.0.0`). This is the case for most commands, though the command's help may not
151:mention that asdf-style syntax is supported. When in doubt, try asdf syntax and see if it works—it probably does.
